WEBVTT


00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.113
You're dead! You're fucking dead!


00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:32.678
I'll get my brother!


00:02:32.759 --> 00:02:37.071
- Jen, come back! Wait!
- Fucking pervert!


00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:41.152
If that was a joke,
it wasn't very fucking funny.


00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:44.037
I'd look out for her brother.
He's a fucking mentalist.


00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:47.030
Jen! Jen!


00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:07.543
- I'll miss you.
- I hate you.


00:04:07.632 --> 00:04:11.103
Can I take this?
This can't still fit you, surely?


00:04:11.193 --> 00:04:13.945
- Get out of my room, Hallam.
- Not without these.


00:04:14.032 --> 00:04:15.750
- Hallam!
- I'm gonna take these,


00:04:15.833 --> 00:04:18.392
- and what if I put these back? Ow!
- Get out of my room.


00:05:33.867 --> 00:05:34.855
Thank you.


00:05:35.866 --> 00:05:39.745
To Australia and great adventures.


00:05:39.827 --> 00:05:41.896
And happy anniversary, Dad and Verity.


00:05:42.786 --> 00:05:44.822
Absent friends.


00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.134
Absent friends.


00:05:53.905 --> 00:05:56.260
Do you know why
we chose this restaurant?


00:05:56.345 --> 00:05:59.621
- It can't be the food.
- I told you to have the veal.


00:05:59.705 --> 00:06:04.698
It was here that Julius first
asked me to help manage the firm.


00:06:04.784 --> 00:06:07.935
You mean when you were the secretary?


00:06:08.024 --> 00:06:10.492
That's right, when I was his secretary.


00:06:10.584 --> 00:06:13.576
- I didn't know that.
- That's because I said no.


00:06:13.664 --> 00:06:14.983
I wasn't ready for it then.


00:06:15.064 --> 00:06:17.623
This afternoon,
I put the same question to Verity,


00:06:17.703 --> 00:06:20.501
- and I'm happy to say she agreed.
- Congratulations.


00:06:24.943 --> 00:06:26.899
When was it you were first asked?


00:06:28.662 --> 00:06:30.619
It must have been
a couple of years ago.


00:06:30.703 --> 00:06:33.341
And was that before or after?


00:06:36.382 --> 00:06:38.771
It wasn't long
before your mother passed away.


00:06:48.981 --> 00:06:52.337
Do you remember what happened later?
Your friend.


00:06:52.421 --> 00:06:56.255
Oh, yes.


00:06:56.341 --> 00:06:58.774
That same day,
an old boyfriend of mine calls up


00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.853
and insists on taking me out
for dinner. Guess where he took me.


00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.852
Can you imagine
what the staff must have thought?


00:07:06.939 --> 00:07:10.376
They probably
thought you were a prostitute.


00:07:18.459 --> 00:07:19.892
Probably.


00:07:25.338 --> 00:07:29.218
- Come to the pub.
- No, thanks. Here's fine.


00:07:29.299 --> 00:07:32.096
You got your binoculars in there?


00:07:32.178 --> 00:07:35.408
- Come to the pub.
- Maybe next time.


00:07:35.498 --> 00:07:38.455
There isn't gonna be a next time.


00:07:43.217 --> 00:07:45.412
You fucking splitter.


00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.768
Night, Mum.


00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.205
Hallam!


00:09:36.329 --> 00:09:38.240
I'm going!


00:09:40.528 --> 00:09:42.599
Bye!


00:09:53.127 --> 00:09:54.481
Lucy!


00:09:57.008 --> 00:10:00.283
Wait! Lucy!


00:10:29.966 --> 00:10:32.559
Hallam, lunch is ready.


00:10:40.965 --> 00:10:42.842
It's very good soup.


00:10:45.524 --> 00:10:47.754
We've been thinking,
now that Lucy's gone,


00:10:47.844 --> 00:10:52.395
it's not good for you to be here
with no one of your own age around.


00:10:53.924 --> 00:10:57.313
Too much time to dwell on things.


00:10:57.403 --> 00:11:00.600
I have some contacts
in the wine trade in London, and...


00:11:00.683 --> 00:11:03.959
You'll have a chance to make
new friends, earn a bit of money,


00:11:04.043 --> 00:11:06.637
learn something you'll enjoy
the rest of your life,


00:11:06.723 --> 00:11:09.442
and it'll be a good
stop-gap before college.


00:11:09.523 --> 00:11:12.400
Actually, I've decided
not to go to college.


00:11:12.482 --> 00:11:16.634
- So what are you going to do?
- I'm staying right here.


00:11:17.562 --> 00:11:20.520
So I'm sorry if that
screws up your plans.


00:12:30.357 --> 00:12:32.586
It's as if this place is still hers.


00:12:32.676 --> 00:12:36.351
We agreed you could make
whatever changes you want, and you are.


00:12:36.436 --> 00:12:39.269
- You know what I want most?
- What?


00:12:44.195 --> 00:12:46.152
- Look, he doesn't hate you.
- He does.


00:12:46.236 --> 00:12:49.750
He doesn't. You just have to be patient.


00:12:53.635 --> 00:12:55.910
I think that
I should go away for a while.


00:12:59.914 --> 00:13:03.065
I'll deal with Hallam. All right?


00:13:24.353 --> 00:13:28.743
- Where's Verity?
- She's gone to see a friend.


00:13:30.952 --> 00:13:32.624
Are you in the dog house?


00:13:34.712 --> 00:13:36.542
What is it, Hallam?


00:13:36.631 --> 00:13:39.304
- I found Mum's old boat in the loch.
- Did you?


00:13:39.391 --> 00:13:43.987
- Good God! I thought it was sunk.
- It had.


00:13:44.071 --> 00:13:47.858
When she took me out in it,
how long was that before she died?


00:13:47.951 --> 00:13:49.828
About a month. Why?


00:13:49.911 --> 00:13:51.947
Were you fucking Verity by then?


00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:57.062
That's what "Fancy a stroll"
was about. Christ, I'm a fool.


00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:00.187
- You haven't answered the question.
- Not even close, Hal.


00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.545
I was busy trying
to keep the show on the road.


00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:05.940
When you found her, had she tied
her hands and weighed herself down?


00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.463
- Where's this coming from?
- People who can swim,


00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:10.938
it's hard to drown. Instincts take over.


00:14:11.029 --> 00:14:16.149
- Who told you that?
- I did some research, all right?


00:14:18.429 --> 00:14:22.866
At the time, I decided to spare you
some of the details from the inquest.


00:14:26.188 --> 00:14:29.863
Before she came out here,


00:14:29.948 --> 00:14:33.656
your mother took
an overdose of sleeping pills.


00:14:37.547 --> 00:14:41.620
- Thanks for fucking telling me.
- I'm sorry.


00:14:42.747 --> 00:14:47.025
I know it's hard, but you
have got to try to pick up the pieces.


00:14:47.107 --> 00:14:49.667
Well, I can see it didn't
take you very long, did it?


00:14:49.747 --> 00:14:52.260
Hal, this won't help.


00:14:56.906 --> 00:14:58.896
So it definitely wasn't an accident?


00:15:00.385 --> 00:15:01.898
No.


00:15:03.305 --> 00:15:04.534
It wasn't.


00:15:39.183 --> 00:15:43.016
Oh, no! I've painted
over his mum's face.


00:15:43.102 --> 00:15:44.820
Paint all over it.


00:15:44.902 --> 00:15:47.780
- Give it here, I'll do it.
- It's a single ticket.


00:15:51.742 --> 00:15:53.698
Fuck off, man. Go!


00:17:09.177 --> 00:17:11.326
<i>- Hallam?
- Lucy?</i>


00:17:14.376 --> 00:17:17.014
<i>- Are you still there? Hello?
- Can you hear me?</i>


00:17:21.016 --> 00:17:25.691
What if someone else gave her the pills?
Spiked her drink or something?


00:17:26.375 --> 00:17:29.287
Well, don't you think
she's capable of it?


00:17:29.375 --> 00:17:31.331
Why is that paranoid?


00:17:33.215 --> 00:17:36.287
Of course I miss you.
Oh, she'd love that.


00:17:36.375 --> 00:17:39.526
She's already twisting Dad's arm
to try and get rid of me.


00:18:48.609 --> 00:18:50.361
Hello!


00:18:53.169 --> 00:18:55.285
I see you've had some visitors.


00:18:55.969 --> 00:18:58.084
- Can I come up?
- No way.


00:19:20.207 --> 00:19:22.083
You left these on your bed.


00:19:25.527 --> 00:19:30.122
"Today, walking past the office,
I saw Dad stroking Verity's back.


00:19:30.207 --> 00:19:32.242
It made me ponder his evening strolls".


00:19:32.326 --> 00:19:34.078
- Not allowed.
- "I followed.


00:19:34.166 --> 00:19:37.953
There she was, bouncing up and down.
I couldn't take my eyes off the dimple


00:19:38.045 --> 00:19:42.800
that appeared on her shoulder
every time she clawed at his neck.


00:19:42.886 --> 00:19:48.482
I hate myself, but I want to
bury my face in that little cushion".


00:19:48.565 --> 00:19:50.680
Give me my diaries back.


00:19:50.765 --> 00:19:53.199
Hallam, you really need to move on.


00:19:53.284 --> 00:19:55.924
I know Julius will feel the same
when he reads these.


00:19:56.005 --> 00:19:57.642
No, they're private diaries!


00:19:57.724 --> 00:20:01.000
So are bedrooms. By volume two,
you peeped in half the village's.


00:20:01.084 --> 00:20:04.281
I wonder what the local paper
would do with that,


00:20:04.364 --> 00:20:07.356
- or the police for that matter.
- The police?


00:20:07.443 --> 00:20:10.163
Wonder what they'll think
when I tell them about you.


00:20:10.244 --> 00:20:11.881
Me?


00:20:13.124 --> 00:20:15.273
Recognise this?


00:20:15.363 --> 00:20:16.591
It's a hammer, Hallam.


00:20:16.683 --> 00:20:20.915
The same hammer that sunk my mother's
boat once you'd drugged her coffee.


00:20:29.002 --> 00:20:31.596
She wanted to die, Hallam.


00:20:31.681 --> 00:20:34.196
You tell me what you did to her!


00:22:03.315 --> 00:22:06.352
It's time to fly the nest, Hallam,


00:22:06.435 --> 00:22:08.390
and I think you know that.


00:22:58.911 --> 00:23:01.141
Spare some change, please.


00:24:29.905 --> 00:24:33.658
- It's a fucking shite hole.
- I didn't want to come here.


00:24:33.744 --> 00:24:37.020
Stick your fucking castle
right up your fucking arse.


00:24:37.104 --> 00:24:39.413
What do you want?


00:24:39.504 --> 00:24:41.699
Thirty, 35?


00:24:42.544 --> 00:24:43.897
Thirty-five?


00:24:46.183 --> 00:24:48.744
Well, go on, fuck off, then!


00:24:48.824 --> 00:24:49.972
Fuck off, then!


00:24:51.223 --> 00:24:53.054
Whoa.


00:24:53.143 --> 00:24:55.896
- What's your name, son?
- Carl.


00:24:55.983 --> 00:24:59.611
- Where's home, Carl?
- I'm staying with a friend.


00:24:59.702 --> 00:25:01.739
Not that gentleman
you were talking to?


00:25:01.822 --> 00:25:05.815
- No.
- So, your friend, what's his address?


00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:35.379
Where the hell is he?


00:26:34.216 --> 00:26:35.773
Mum!


00:27:53.610 --> 00:27:55.168
Can I help you?


00:28:00.249 --> 00:28:02.479
Do you have any jobs, please?


00:28:02.569 --> 00:28:05.561
Sorry, we use an agency.
I can give you their details.


00:28:05.649 --> 00:28:07.128
Thanks.


00:28:15.328 --> 00:28:17.319
Why are you staring at me?


00:28:17.408 --> 00:28:21.447
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to. I've never
been for a job interview before,


00:28:21.528 --> 00:28:25.566
and I was just wondering if you could
give me some advice on how to do it.


00:28:25.647 --> 00:28:29.402
- I'm sorry?
- Would you...?


00:28:29.487 --> 00:28:32.638
Could you throw a couple
of practise questions at me, just...


00:28:32.727 --> 00:28:34.319
...just for practise?


00:28:37.447 --> 00:28:41.599
- How desperate are you for work?
- Pretty desperate.


00:28:41.687 --> 00:28:45.565
Well, the highest turnover in jobs
is usually in kitchen porters.


00:28:45.646 --> 00:28:49.116
- OK. I'll be a kitchen porter.
- Why do you think you'd be suitable?


00:28:49.206 --> 00:28:52.118
Well, it's what I've wanted to do
ever since I was a kid.


00:28:52.205 --> 00:28:53.923
Sit down.


00:28:56.485 --> 00:28:59.602
Don't tell people
what you think they want to hear.


00:28:59.685 --> 00:29:02.404
- Just be yourself.
- OK.


00:29:02.485 --> 00:29:05.522
I'm very enthusiastic
and I'm a quick learner,


00:29:05.605 --> 00:29:07.755
and I'll work days, nights, weekends,


00:29:07.844 --> 00:29:09.914
any overtime you want
for no extra money.


00:29:10.004 --> 00:29:14.316
It would be illegal for you
to work overtime for no extra money.


00:29:14.404 --> 00:29:16.793
Well, give me a week's trial,
a day's trial.


00:29:16.884 --> 00:29:19.034
I want a chance
to get a foot on the ladder.


00:29:19.124 --> 00:29:21.922
If everything works out,
you won't pay agency fees.


00:29:22.004 --> 00:29:24.915
That's a win-win situation for you.


00:29:30.963 --> 00:29:34.955
Remember what I said about
the fast turnover in kitchen porters?


00:29:36.003 --> 00:29:38.836
You're about to meet the exception.


00:29:39.882 --> 00:29:43.511
- Cutlery, handles up.
- Right.


00:29:43.602 --> 00:29:44.875
Go on.


00:29:47.881 --> 00:29:52.432
Hey, hey, hey! What is the hurry?
Trying to show me up on your first day?


00:29:52.521 --> 00:29:54.159
No.


00:29:54.241 --> 00:29:58.473
I fucking hate this job,
but it's my job.


00:29:58.561 --> 00:30:00.040
Do you understand?


00:30:01.641 --> 00:30:03.471
I killed a man once.


00:30:03.560 --> 00:30:05.950
Smashed his skull on a pier.


00:30:07.080 --> 00:30:08.593
Just so you know.


00:30:28.279 --> 00:30:30.838
You take the rest. I'm off for a smoke.


00:32:51.029 --> 00:32:54.498
Don't make friends with the chefs,
otherwise they'll want favours.


00:32:54.588 --> 00:32:56.419
But don't get on their bad side,


00:32:56.508 --> 00:33:00.296
or you'll be cleaning out
the fat fryer on a quiet Thursday.


00:33:01.028 --> 00:33:05.067
They're all cunts anyway.
Except TJ. He's OK.


00:33:05.148 --> 00:33:07.058
Even if he is a fucking bullshitter.


00:33:07.147 --> 00:33:11.186
Have you ever met an African over here
who wasn't a brain surgeon over there?


00:33:11.267 --> 00:33:13.985
Are you listening to me?


00:33:15.907 --> 00:33:18.340
Yes, of course.


00:33:18.426 --> 00:33:21.543
Brain surgeon. African. Cunt.


00:33:21.626 --> 00:33:24.538
Aye, cunt.


00:33:40.265 --> 00:33:43.734
Reach out. One, two.
One. Right knee.


00:38:46.842 --> 00:38:49.437
- Hey! Ho!
- Raymond!


00:38:49.522 --> 00:38:51.114
- Hey!
- Hey!


00:38:51.202 --> 00:38:55.161
Oh-ho! That's gonna cost you.


00:38:55.242 --> 00:38:57.358
- Really?
- Yeah.


00:39:01.081 --> 00:39:04.870
- Are you serious?
- Absolutely.


00:39:12.601 --> 00:39:14.159
Come on. You're losing.


00:39:20.241 --> 00:39:21.639
That's ¡Ì4.


00:39:25.720 --> 00:39:28.757
- Do you mind if I take a break?
- Do what the fuck you like.

